OL,3,CThe prime minister is on holiday, so
OL,4,Cwho is in charge?
OL,6,FIn the UK, there is no constitutional
OL,7,Frequirement for a deputy or caretaker
OL,8,Fprime minister, meaning that it is not
OL,9,Fessential for a prime minister to
OL,10,Fappoint one.
OL,12,FInstead, titles such as Deputy Prime
OL,13,FMinister, First Secretary of State or
OL,14,FChancellor of the Duchy of Lancaster
OL,15,Fcan be given to a member of the
OL,16,Fcabinet who may fulfil the role as the
OL,17,Fpremier's number two in some capacity.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
