OL,3,CThe prime minister is on holiday, so
OL,4,Cwho is in charge?
OL,6,F"I'm not going to criticise a
OL,7,Fpolitician for taking a holiday," she
OL,8,Fsaid. "I'm not going to criticise Andy
OL,9,FBurnham for that.
OL,11,F"It's children's school holidays, my
OL,12,Fchildren are on a holiday, I hope that
OL,13,Feverybody should be taking a break."
OL,15,FBadenoch was more concerned about
OL,16,FBurnham not having to face parliament
OL,17,Ffor the first time as prime minister
OL,18,Funtil MPs return in September.
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/10
